.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bap 1  "bap 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
bap \- Bap Runtime: a V8 JavaScript and TypeScript runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbap\fR [\fB\-\-metrics\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bap Runtime: a V8 JavaScript and TypeScript runtime
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fI<METRICS>\fR [default: pretty]
metrics report format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pretty
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
tracing filter, e.g. debug
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bap\-run(1)
Run a JavaScript or TypeScript file (bare `bap run` picks one)
.TP
bap\-repl(1)
Start an interactive REPL
.TP
bap\-init(1)
Scaffold a bap.json for this project
.TP
bap\-setup(1)
Configure this machine: completions and man pages
.TP
bap\-upgrade(1)
Update bap to the latest GitHub release
.TP
bap\-install(1)
Install packages into node_modules (reads package.json with no specs)
.TP
bap\-add(1)
Add packages to package.json and install them
.TP
bap\-remove(1)
Remove packages from package.json and node_modules
.TP
bap\-doctor(1)
Diagnose a project\*(Aqs compatibility with Bap
.TP
bap\-bench(1)
Measure script latency across pinned isolates
.TP
bap\-report(1)
Print measured reports
.TP
bap\-inspect(1)
Inspect runtime artifacts
.TP
bap\-complete(1)
Emit a shell completion script for bap
.TP
bap\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Run `bap <command> \-\-help` for details. New here? Try `bap init` then `bap run`.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
